---
source: crates/togi/tests/cli.rs
expression: "help_output(& [\"--help\"])"
---
Polyglot formatter and linter for data science projects: R, Python, Quarto/Markdown, and SQL behind one stable interface.

togi routes every file to the right underlying tool and manages its own copies of those tools, downloading them into a private cache on first use. No configuration is required; a project togi.toml overrides only what it sets.

Usage: togi [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  format       Format project files in place (R, Python, Quarto, SQL, Markdown) [aliases: fmt]
  lint         Report lint violations across the project
  tools        Manage togi-installed formatter/linter tools (advanced)
  completions  Generate shell completions
  version      Print the togi version and the tool versions baked into this release
  upgrade      Upgrade togi to the latest release
  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -v, --verbose
          Show more detail (underlying commands, tool names)

  -q, --quiet
          Suppress all output except errors

      --no-color
          Disable colored output

      --config <PATH>
          Use this config file instead of discovering togi.toml

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
